  "releaseTestingSchematic": {
    "labels": [
      "Final CAR-T product",
      "Safety and identity: product-specific tests",
      "Viability, CAR expression and vector-related attributes",
      "Timing and sampling depend on the workflow"
    ],
    "captions": [
      "1 · A cell-product lot is sampled for specified quality checks; assay requirements and acceptance criteria depend on the product and development stage",
      "2 · Sterility, mycoplasma and endotoxin assays assess specified contamination risks; identity testing and cell tracking address different questions. Flow cytometry can measure viability and CAR expression",
      "3 · Where relevant, vector-copy and replication-competent-virus tests assess vector-related attributes. Potency assays measure a specified biological activity; cytokine release and target-cell killing are different readouts",
      "4 · Test duration and sampling needs depend on the workflow. A release result supports a lot-quality decision; its relationship to clinical outcomes needs product-specific evidence"
    ]
  }
